## Outcome
Reread after the recorded proof. `clerk-deliver` is the one fixture command. `app/librarian.py` loads `app/clerk_seam.py` only for that command and passes its own context module, so a refusal stays `context.Stop`. The seam pins `app/clerk-seam.json` and does not start Clerk until the hash matches. Job, checks, claim, and recorded return come from `show --json`, schema `clerk-handoff-inspection/2`. The seam does not read raw events or inbox text.

While the job is claimed, `claim --resume` is the public token check: the three lines must match the inspection token and the instruction hash. Resume is not called for a returned job. That replay uses the inspection token and still checks the actor, the instructions, and the stored job identity. On every existing delivery, `link.bridge_job_sha256` must equal `provenance.job_sha256` and the current job bytes. The worker call is `worker_bridge.perform`. The receipt check is `worker_bridge._read_stored_receipt`. A collected `done` is exclusive-copied into the Clerk outbox and returned with one evidence line. Exit 3 and exit 4 keep the claim and the bridge evidence, do not return the job, and do not relaunch. `bridge-recover` remains a separate command. An identical completed replay launches nothing. There is no seam ledger and no exactly-once claim. `run` stays refused. No model profile is configured.

Two defects were fixed before this recorded run. Guarding the pinned Clerk path with `guard_workspace_path` refused the lab file as a source tree; the pin now resolves under the code root, refuses a link, and refuses a hash mismatch before any subprocess. Resolving an outbox junction made a linked name look like an escape; an existing link, junction, or extra hard link is attention at exit 4 and is left in place.

The recorded suites are one disposable copy, `C:/Users/misg/AppData/Local/Temp/seam0510-repo`, using these bytes and no Git directory until the placement test planted a marker and removed it. `test_clerk_seam.py` exit 0: pass 30, expected-refusal 18, skip 1, fail 0. The skip is the file symlink, WinError 1314. Its fresh-process demo recorded receipt `3b08575c251359118482fbdcc3927130031baf348b2e5803d49c8e0b8278b594`, artifact `0c07187ea6d064441225b3cba26a7b1e8bc702fcf332b457dae8e26892ba68a6`, one launch, and replay `already-recorded`. `test_entry.py` exit 0: pass 12, expected-refusal 46, skip 1, fail 0. `test_prime_tools.py -v` exit 0: Ran 12 tests in 14.646s, OK (skipped=1). `test_worker_bridge.py` exit 0: pass 38, expected-refusal 27, skip 1, fail 0. Those skips are the same WinError 1314 file-symlink case. Source-before `librarian.py` and `README.md` are unchanged. No shared Git write. Review is not performed. This slot authorizes no further work.
